{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfun5uZXzsfcTxbWgfnSs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Not directly. `this.schedule()`, `getSchedules()`, and `cancelSchedule()` are methods on the `Agent` class. They depend on `Agent`'s internals: a SQLite-backed schedules table in the Durable Object's storage, and its own `alarm()` handler that dispatches to your callback methods. As far as I know, the SDK doesn't export them as a standalone utility you can attach to an arbitrary `DurableObject`.\n\nYou have two options:\n\n- **Extend `Agent`.** `Agent` is itself a Durable Object subclass, so switching your class to `extends Agent` is usually low-cost. Your binding needs to use SQLite storage (`new_sqlite_classes` in the migration). Avoid overriding `alarm()` yourself, or call `super.alarm()` if you do.\n- **Build it yourself in the plain DO.** Store pending tasks in `ctx.storage.sql` or KV, then use `ctx.storage.setAlarm()` for the earliest due time. In `alarm()`, run whatever is due and re-arm the alarm. For cron expressions, add a parser such as `cron-schedule`.\n\nCheck the current Agents SDK docs in case a standalone scheduler has been added since I last saw it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2254,"cache_read_input_tokens":535,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2254},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fddd370e-cc6b-41db-8673-190ebb57d2a7","uuid":"d0ed8551-feaf-4829-8d25-9bbc5d28b41b","timestamp":"2026-10-11T03:57:39.796Z","request_id":"req_011Cfun5uNcR3kkoKikBEkHf"}
